   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report to the relevant regulator any thermal incident involving fire, smoke, injury, property damage, emergency response, or a safety-related shutdown within 24 hours of learning of it. Other confirmed thermal incidents must be reported within 5 business days. The manufacturer must notify affected owners within 5 business days of confirming a material safety risk, with instructions to reduce risk and contact support.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report to the relevant regulator any thermal incident involving fire, smoke, injury, property damage, emergency response, or a safety-related shutdown within 24 hours of learning of it. Other confirmed thermal incidents must be reported within 5 business days. Reports must include the unit/model, event description, known consequences, and any immediate corrective action; updates are due as material facts become known. The manufacturer must notify affected owners within 5 business days of confirming a material safety risk, with instructions to reduce risk and contact support. Imminent risks require customer notice within 24 hours."
  },
