   "rule_summary": "The maximum permitted failure rate is 7%. Models exceeding 5% must complete corrective action and retesting; models exceeding 7% must not be sold until corrective action is completed and regulators approve retesting at or below 7%. Customers purchasing a model must receive its test results and compliance status; individual companies' per-model failure rates must not be published to the general public.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: permanent_limit_pct",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a documented sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a regulator-recognized protocol and a representative sample before sale and after material design changes. Manufacturers must provide regulators with complete per-model test methods, sample sizes, measured failure rates, and results. Customers purchasing a model must receive its test results and compliance status; individual companies’ per-model failure rates must not be published to the general public. The maximum permitted failure rate is 7%. Models exceeding 5% must complete corrective action and retesting; models exceeding 7% must not be sold until corrective action is completed and regulators approve retesting at or below 7%. Regulators may require an immediate stop-sale or other protective action where evidence indicates imminent risk."
  },
