   "final_rule_text": "New units must include a remote emergency shut-off function that can be activated by the customer and, where necessary to address an imminent safety risk, by the manufacturer with prompt customer notification. Manufacturers must provide clear instructions and safeguards against unauthorized activation. For installed units lacking this function, manufacturers must provide an approved retrofit or equivalent risk-reduction measure within 72 months of adoption, prioritizing units with elevated risk. Regulators may approve alternative risk-reduction measures where a retrofit is infeasible or would create additional safety risks."
