   "final_rule_text": "Before purchase, customers must receive clear written information on thermal hazards, installation and placement requirements, emergency steps, warranty/support contacts, and how to check for safety notices. Manufacturers must promptly notify owners of confirmed material risks and provide updated instructions and remedies. A manufacturer must initiate a regulator-supervised recall when a model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in any rolling 12-month period, or when the regulator determines that a defect presents an equivalent imminent risk. The recall must provide effective corrective action, such as repair, replacement, or refund. Regulators determine whether sales may resume after corrective action addresses the risk. Incidents and recall rates must be calculated by model using documented installed-unit counts."
